  (text "CAN (ISO 11898-2 high speed): J1939 / FMS on trucks, OBD-II (ISO 15765-4) on cars, any 11/29-bit CAN up to 1 Mbit/s.\nESP32 TWAI controller (classic CAN only, one bus): TX = GPIO33, RX = GPIO15 (strapping pin MTDO; an idle bus holds RXD high = default boot).\nU1001 TJA1051T/3: VCC 5 V (+5V), VIO 3.3 V logic, CANH/CANL rated +/-58 V, so a 12/24/28 V miswire is survived.\nD1001 SZNUP3105L at the J1 pins: 32 V working voltage (does not conduct on a 28 V truck supply), 30 pF per line, 350 W 8/20 us.\nJP1001 TERM: 120 R across the bus. Leave OPEN when tapping a vehicle bus (it is already terminated); bridge only at a bus end.\nJP1002 LISTEN-ONLY: bridged = S high = transceiver silent (receive only, guaranteed by hardware). Open = normal (S pulled low inside).\nFirmware can also use TWAI listen-only mode; OBD-II requests and ACKs need normal mode."
    (at 88.9 40.64 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "3ad2f587-9408-41de-96e5-596ca64e8a81")
  )
